= Classification — Simple =

'''Classification''' means putting things into categories.

For example:
* sorting books by subject;
* deciding whether an email is spam;
* classifying an animal by species;
* putting a medical case into a diagnosis category.

Classification needs rules or criteria.

A [[Taxonomy/Simple|taxonomy]] can organize the categories used for classification.

The two are related but different:

* taxonomy organizes categories;
* classification assigns things to them.

Computers can classify using hand-written rules or learned statistical models.

A classification can be technically consistent and still use bad categories, so the categories themselves also need to make sense.

